# The update package is signed over its exact bytes. core.autocrlf is true on
# the machine that publishes these, so a file git decides is text gets its LF
# turned into CRLF on checkout -- and a payload one byte different from the one
# that was signed is one every install downloads and then refuses, with no way
# for the person to tell why.
#
# Git's binary detection got this right unprompted, which is not the same as it
# being guaranteed. This makes it guaranteed.
updates/** -text -diff
*.exe      -text -diff
